# Gradle / build output
build/
.gradle/
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

# Dev run directory (worlds, logs, configs)
run/
logs/

# IDE
.idea/
*.iml

# The one dependency that cannot come from maven (see libs/README.md for why, and for how to build
# it). Its jar is All Rights Reserved and must never be committed. The glob is doubled up so it also
# covers libs/backup/, where an older build is kept to roll back to: a single-star pattern only
# matches the directory's own children, so a jar one level down would have slipped into the commit.
libs/**/*.jar

# Where tools/fetch-thaumaturge.* checks Thaumaturge out. CI points it at the workspace root so the
# path is stable for the run; it is deliberately not cached (see .github/workflows/build.yml, which
# explains why a Thaumaturge checkout must not end up in this repository's Actions cache). Not a
# dot-directory: Gradle refuses to configure a project whose directory name begins with a dot.
thaumaturge-src/

# JVM crash logs
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log
*.log

# Working notes stay out of the repository and live on disk only - the same rule the 2.0-Renewed
# branch's .gitignore states for docs/. _scratch holds what a working copy accumulates and a clone
# has no use for: the plan documents, the 2.0-Renewed archive, the diagnostic source set, and the
# one-off scripts that have already done their job. Nothing in the build reads any of it.
_scratch/
PLAN*.md
Thaumic-Energistics-CE-2.0-Renewed.zip
